The correct answer is **__seven__**. [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/36f36cd5ece4186095afcf2ffbfb7b80cc04b6c2e3226e7477a419a9fbc96f85.png] **__Key Points__**


• **Article 19 **of the Constitution of India had originally guaranteed** seven fundamental rights**.

• **Article 19: **Protection of certain rights regarding freedom of speech etc;

• **Article 19(1):** All citizen shall have the right 


• **Article 19(1)(a) **- To freedom of speech and expression;

• Article 19(1)(b) - To assemble peaceably and without arms;

• Article 19(1)(c) - To form associations or unions;

